  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ミズワラビ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%9F%E3%82%BA%E3%83%AF%E3%83%A9%E3%83%93",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106991171,
      "text": "ミズワラビ は、シダ植物門ホウライシダ科に属するシダである。分類によってはイノモトソウ科やミズワラビ科 (Ceratopteridaceae) とする場合もある。シダとしては珍しい水草で、水中、あるいは湿地に生える。熱帯地方に広く分布し、日本では本州中部以南に分布する。ただし現在では日本本土のものを同属の別種（ヒメミズワラビ）としており、本種に当たるのは南西諸島のものだけである。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Ceratopteris thalictroides」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceratopteris_thalictroides",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1378662230,
      "text": "Ceratopteris thalictroides is a fern species belonging to the genus Ceratopteris, one of only two genera of the subfamily Parkerioideae of the family Pteridaceae."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Ceratopteris thalictroides」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceratopteris_thalictroides#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1378662230,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "It grows best in soil with a pH reading of 5-9 and in very high amounts of light. It usually grows quickly.\nC. thalictroides can benefit (like all aquatic plants) from the addition of CO2. The plant's reproductive technique is similar to other ferns. Small adventitious plantlets are grown on the mother plant and are then released when ready.\nIt can provide useful shade to shyer fish and small fry. The dense roots are said to take nutrients out of the water, helping to prevent the growth of algae.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
